     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hello\r\nDistancers, I am running CDS model with a group covariate (formula=~size)in R\r\nDistance but I think I am overestimating densities. The models with better\r\nadjustment give me very high values of density, the values are also are remarkably\r\ndifferent from the data obtained previously by Distance for Windows (density approximately of  22 indiv/km2). <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I have run the\r\nmodels detailed below: <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">oct12&lt;-read.csv(&quot;oct12R.csv&quot;,\r\nheader=TRUE, dec = &quot;.&quot;, sep=&quot;,&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">par(mfrow=c(1,2))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">hist(oct12$distance,main=&quot;&quot;,xlab=&quot;Distance\r\n(m)&quot;) #histograma de frec de distancias, en km<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">hist(oct12$size,main=&quot;&quot;,xlab=&quot;Cluster\r\nsize&quot;) #histograma de frec de tamanios de grupo<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"># plots of\r\ndistance vs. cluster size<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">par(mfrow=c(1,1))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">plot(oct12$distance,\r\nnov10$groupsize, main=&quot;&quot;, xlab=&quot;Distance (m)&quot;,ylab=&quot;Group\r\nsize&quot;, pch=19, cex=0.5, col=gray(0.7))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">hr12&lt;-ds(oct12,\r\nkey=&quot;hr&quot;, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size,convert.units = 0.001) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(hr12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">gof_ds(hr12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">plot(hr12,\r\nnc = 12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">hr12_980&lt;-ds(oct12,\r\nkey=&quot;hr&quot;,truncation=980, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size,convert.units=\r\n0.001) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(hr12_980)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">gof_ds(hr12_980)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">plot(hr12_980,\r\nnc = 12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">hn12&lt;-ds(oct12,\r\nkey=&quot;hn&quot;, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size,convert.units = 0.001) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(hn12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">gof_ds(hn12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">plot(hn12,\r\nnc = 12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">hn12_980&lt;-ds(oct12,\r\nkey=&quot;hn&quot;,truncation=980, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size, convert.units\r\n= 0.001) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(hn12_980)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">gof_ds(hn12_980)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">plot(hn12_980,\r\nnc = 12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">hr12_920&lt;-ds(oct12,\r\nkey=&quot;hr&quot;,truncation=920, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size</span>,convert.units = 0.001)</p